From 7714db5d62324b606c8ca928530ebdf25bb3aefe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:18:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 473/474] test: linked worktrees pass the real-home guard;
 spawn-refusal test is Linux-only [daveey]

Running scripts/run_tests.sh from a hermes-core-wt worktree failed 206 tests
in tests/hermes_cli (-k "kanban or session"); 296 of 298 failure blocks were
"TEST BUG: file I/O against the REAL hermes home: <home>/hermes-agent/.git/
worktrees/<name>/hermes-update-pull".

Why 1: the CLI's early-recovery probe stats the interrupted-update marker in
  the running checkout's git dir (_early_recovery._git_dir).
Why 2: for a linked worktree that git dir is the target of its .git file,
  under the home's hermes-agent/.git/worktrees/ (hermes-core-wt's layout).
Why 3: home_io_guard exempts the checkout tree itself (a plain clone's .git
  is inside it) but not a linked worktree's git dir outside the tree.
Why not caught: CI runs from a plain clone; only local worktree runs hit it,
  and those false failures read as "pre-existing" noise and hid real ones.
Fix: linked_worktree_git_dirs() adds the worktree's own git dir to the same
  exemption (only that dir; the rest of the home stays refused). Result:
  206 failed -> 9, the remainder outside the kanban sync work.

test_infrastructure_spawn_refusal_never_charges_the_card drives the systemd
restart-safe scope refusal; restart_safe_gateway_child_argv returns
in_process on non-Linux, so on macOS the refusal never happens and the test
failed. Marked platforms("linux"); verified passing on Linux (hub, clean
clone of 4cfc27bc).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
